BT /F2 17 Tf 54 730.0 Td (Third-Party & Supply-Chain Risk Management Policy) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 697.0 Td (1. Purpose and Scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 674.0 Td (Hewlett Packard Enterprise \(HPE\) depends on an extensive ecosystem of third parties - cloud) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 660.0 Td (providers such as AWS and Microsoft Azure, enterprise software vendors including SAP and Salesforce,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 646.0 Td (identity providers like Okta, and hardware manufacturing partners such as Foxconn. This Third-Party) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 632.0 Td (and Supply-Chain Risk Management Policy establishes the requirements governing how HPE identifies,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 618.0 Td (assesses, and oversees every vendor, supplier, service provider, and outsourcing arrangement across) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 604.0 Td (its supply chain. It applies to all business units, procurement teams, and personnel who engage,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 590.0 Td (contract with, or manage external parties on behalf of HPE.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 570.0 Td (The objective of this program is to ensure that risks introduced by third parties - including) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 556.0 Td (cybersecurity, operational, financial, privacy, regulatory, and reputational risks - are managed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 542.0 Td (consistently throughout the entire vendor lifecycle, from onboarding through offboarding.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 516.0 Td (2. Governance and Ownership) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 493.0 Td (The Third-Party Risk Management \(TPRM\) function, operating under the Chief Information Security) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 479.0 Td (Officer and Chief Procurement Officer, owns this policy. Business owners act as relationship) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 465.0 Td (managers accountable for the day-to-day performance and risk posture of each supplier they sponsor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 451.0 Td (The TPRM Committee reviews escalations, approves exceptions, and reports aggregate supply-chain risk) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 437.0 Td (to executive leadership and the Board Risk Committee on a quarterly basis.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 411.0 Td (3. Vendor Inventory and Identification) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 388.0 Td (HPE maintains a centralized vendor inventory \(the authoritative supplier catalog\) that records every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 374.0 Td (third party with access to HPE systems, data, facilities, or that delivers goods and services) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 360.0 Td (material to operations. No engagement may proceed until the vendor is formally identified and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 346.0 Td (registered on this list. The inventory captures ownership, data classification handled, spend,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 332.0 Td (contract dates, and the assigned risk tier. Procurement reconciles the catalog against) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 318.0 Td (accounts-payable records at least annually to detect unregistered or "shadow" vendors.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 292.0 Td (4. Vendor Tiering and Criticality Classification) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 269.0 Td (Every third party is subject to risk-based tiering. During onboarding, TPRM performs an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 255.0 Td (inherent-risk classification that categorizes the supplier by criticality using factors such as data) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 241.0 Td (sensitivity, system access, business dependency, regulatory exposure, and substitutability. This) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 227.0 Td (risk-rating produces a tier:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 207.0 Td (- Tier 1 - Critical: Vendors whose failure would materially disrupt HPE operations or expose) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 193.0 Td (  regulated/confidential data \(e.g., AWS, Microsoft, Okta, Foxconn\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 179.0 Td (- Tier 2 - Important: Vendors handling significant but recoverable services \(e.g., SAP,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 165.0 Td (  Salesforce\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 151.0 Td (- Tier 3 - Limited: Vendors with minimal access or impact.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 131.0 Td (The assigned tier determines the depth of due diligence, contractual rigor, and monitoring frequency) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 117.0 Td (applied.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 91.0 Td (5. Due Diligence and Assessment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 68.0 Td (Before contract execution, each vendor undergoes due diligence proportionate to its tier. HPE issues) Tj ET
endstream
