BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738.0 Td (a standardized security and privacy assessment questionnaire \(aligned to ISO 27001, SOC 2, and NIST) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 724.0 Td (frameworks\) and reviews supporting evidence such as audit reports, penetration-test summaries,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 710.0 Td (financial statements, and certifications. Tier 1 suppliers additionally receive an on-site or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 696.0 Td (virtual control review and, where applicable, a supply-chain integrity assessment covering hardware) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 682.0 Td (provenance and counterfeit prevention. Assessment findings must be remediated or formally) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 668.0 Td (risk-accepted before onboarding is approved.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 642.0 Td (6. Contractual Controls) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 619.0 Td (All third-party relationships must be governed by written contracts and agreements that codify HPE's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 605.0 Td (risk requirements. Contracts must include, at minimum: data protection and confidentiality clauses,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 591.0 Td (defined service-level agreements \(SLAs\) with performance and availability commitments,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 577.0 Td (breach-notification obligations, compliance with applicable laws, a right-to-audit clause enabling) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 563.0 Td (HPE to verify controls, and clearly documented exit and termination provisions. Legal and TPRM) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 549.0 Td (jointly approve deviations from standard clauses. SLAs are tracked against measured performance, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 535.0 Td (persistent breaches trigger escalation.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 509.0 Td (7. Subcontractor and Fourth-Party Oversight) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 486.0 Td (Vendors frequently rely on their own subcontractors, creating fourth-party and nth-party) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 472.0 Td (dependencies that can propagate risk into HPE's supply chain. Contracts must require suppliers to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 458.0 Td (disclose material subcontractors, flow down equivalent security and privacy obligations, and obtain) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 444.0 Td (HPE approval before engaging fourth parties that handle HPE data. TPRM maps concentration risk - for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 430.0 Td (example, multiple critical vendors depending on the same underlying cloud infrastructure - and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 416.0 Td (factors this exposure into resilience planning.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 390.0 Td (8. Ongoing and Continuous Monitoring) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 367.0 Td (Third-party risk is managed continuously, not only at onboarding. HPE performs periodic reassessment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 353.0 Td (of each vendor on a cadence driven by tier - Tier 1 annually, Tier 2 biennially, and Tier 3 on a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 339.0 Td (risk-triggered basis. Continuous monitoring includes external security-rating feeds,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 325.0 Td (threat-intelligence and breach alerts, SLA performance reviews, and re-issued questionnaires.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 311.0 Td (Material changes - a data breach, ownership change, adverse audit finding, or degraded rating -) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 297.0 Td (trigger an off-cycle review and, where warranted, remediation plans or tier reclassification.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 271.0 Td (9. Exit, Termination, and Contingency Strategy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 248.0 Td (Every critical engagement must have a documented exit and transition strategy defined before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 234.0 Td (onboarding. Offboarding procedures ensure secure return or destruction of HPE data, revocation of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 220.0 Td (access, knowledge transfer, and orderly service migration. For Tier 1 suppliers, HPE maintains) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 206.0 Td (contingency and business-continuity plans - including identified alternate providers or in-sourcing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 192.0 Td (options - so that termination, insolvency, or sustained SLA failure does not disrupt operations.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 166.0 Td (10. Enforcement and Review) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 143.0 Td (Non-compliance with this policy may result in engagement suspension and disciplinary action. This) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 129.0 Td (policy is reviewed at least annually, or upon significant regulatory or business change, by the TPRM) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 115.0 Td (Committee.) Tj ET
